{"assets":["/statement-assets/cb58729534214306c66e5b096d6b23e313044fce492fc9321a9a67f8649091e0.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1917","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Construct Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array of integers $$$l_1, l_2, \\dots, l_n$$$ and an integer $$$d$$$. Is it possible to construct a tree satisfying the following three conditions?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The tree contains $$$n + 1$$$ nodes. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The length of the $$$i$$$-th edge is equal to $$$l_i$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The (weighted) diameter of the tree is equal to $$$d$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 250$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$, $$$d$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 2000, 1 \\leq d \\leq 2000$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$l_1, l_2, \\dots, l_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq l_i \\leq d$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output $$$\\texttt{Yes}$$$ if it is possible to construct a tree that satisfies all the conditions, and $$$\\texttt{No}$$$ otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can print the letters in any case (upper or lower)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n4 10\n1 2 3 4\n4 7\n1 4 3 4\n6 18\n2 4 3 7 6 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYes\nNo\nYes\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Below, you are given the illustrations of trees for the first and third test cases. One of the diameters is highlighted by coloring its edges in red."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/cb58729534214306c66e5b096d6b23e313044fce492fc9321a9a67f8649091e0.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1917F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1917/problem/F"}